        },
        {
          "type": "rubric",
          "source": "Hymn - The Conversion of S. Norbert",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            573
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              573
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "matins-b0006",
          "verification": "visual-review"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "O blessed Saint! While yet unborn, A voice Divine decreed for thee; ”Thou’lt bear, through many a life-long storm, The priest’s and bishop’s dignity”. Yet worldly glory wooed thy heart, And thou, of noble race, didst turn Away from thine eternal part To seek the fair, false lights that burn In royal halls of earth. But lo! These halls are trembling ’neath the power Of Him Who stoops to thee, to show Thou shalt be His. Alas! That hour Thou’rt faltering still. The voice of fame, Its flattery, in thine ear is sweet. Again thy God thy heart must claim And sweetly stay thy wand’ring feet. May we, like thee, shun worldly praise, In worldly paths no longer roam, But tread the peaceful, heavenward ways, Till angels come to lead us home.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            573
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              573
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "matins-b0007",
          "verification": "visual-review"
        },
        {
          "type": "rubric",
          "source": "Antiphon",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            573
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              573
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "matins-b0008",
          "verification": "visual-review"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Being found in the rugged paths of vice by the Guardian of the city, stayed by lightning stroke, he puts off the old man, and is clothed with the first robe of innocence. He who was dead lives again; he who was lost is found.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            573
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              573
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "matins-b0009",
          "verification": "visual-review"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "℣. Pray for us, O S. Norbert,",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            573
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              573
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "matins-b0010",
          "verification": "visual-review"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "℟. That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            573
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              573
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "matins-b0011",
          "verification": "visual-review"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Let us pray,",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            573
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              573
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "matins-b0012",
          "verification": "visual-review"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Awake, O Lord, in Thy Church the Spirit by Whom S. Norbert, Thy Confessor and Bishop, was guided, in order that, filled with the same Spirit, we may love what he loved, and live as he taught us. Through Christ, Our Lord. Amen.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            573
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              573
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "matins-b0013",
          "verification": "visual-review"
        }
      ]
