          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "terce-b0006",
          "verification": "visual-review"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "In token of her constant love The glorious Queen of Heaven above Clothes thee in white, that thou may’st be A witness to her purity.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            574
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              574
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "terce-b0007",
          "verification": "visual-review"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "S. Austin gives his hallowed Rule To train thy followers in that school Of holy life. And robed in light, The Saviour meets the raptured sight, To show, by seven-fold rays, the place Where Norbert’s band – a chosen race, Shall dwell, as oft by Heaven foretold, In lone Prémontré’s blessed fold. S. Norbert, who the world disdained, Pray that we may, with hearts unstained, Walk in the light of purity, And thus the heavenly nuptials see.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            574
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              574
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "terce-b0008",
          "verification": "visual-review"
        },
        {
          "type": "rubric",
          "source": "Antiphon",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            574
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              574
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "terce-b0009",
          "verification": "visual-review"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "He sought a place wherein he might fitly live and walk in the path of God, where there are different ways that lead to Him. When, therefore, he had found the vale of Prémontré, he cried out: ”This is the spot which the Lord has chosen for us.”",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            574
          ],
          "translation": {
            "kind": "source-English",
            "sourcePages": [
              574
            ]
          },
          "alignment": "single-language",
          "id": "terce-b0010",
          "verification": "visual-review"
        },
        {
