          "verification": "visual-review"
        },
        {
          "type": "prayer",
          "source": "Death summons thee, but do not fear, The voice of Jesus soundeth near; ”Come, my beloved, take thy rest, Come, for thou shalt be crowned and blessed”. Thy combat o’er, thy work is done. The arms of Mary and her Son Are clasped around thee. Thou dost bear The olive and the lily fair, And thus, beyond the distant star, Thou’rt borne to heavenly courts afar, Oh! may we win that peaceful rest, We pray, who in thy joy are blest.",
          "english": null,
          "sourcePages": [
            576
          ],
